{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: let the step commands take their projection from the resident when --server is given.\n\nWhy. gs promise, gs artifact, gs review-request, gs land, gs work --next and the preflight in gs state, batch, ratify and supersede open with snapshotWithProgress, which verifies the whole log locally even when --server names a resident that already holds the verified projection. At depth 23,500 that is about five minutes per command on this machine, and each of the Dependabot lanes on 2026-09-17 paid it five or six times. gs status --json --server already does the right thing: fetchFullStatus reads /v0/status, whose durable field is an app.Snapshot, and validateRemoteFrontier accepts it only when its head equals the local sequence ref before and after the read. The step commands need nothing the status snapshot lacks: they build their indexes from Projection.Statements and Projection.Commitments.\n\nOutcome. When --server is given, every step and preflighting command sources its snapshot from the resident's /v0/status, accepted under the same frontier validation gs status uses, and falls back to the local audit, saying so on stderr, when the resident is unreachable, serves another genesis, or is not at the local ref. The projection a command judges against and the resident that folds the act are then the same world. The local audit path is unchanged when --server is absent.","body":{"branch":"request/resident-projection","conditions":"1. One shared opener gives gs promise, artifact, review-request, land, work --next and the preflight of state, batch, ratify and supersede a resident-sourced snapshot under --server, validated with the existing frontier check, with local audit as the stated fallback. 2. Tests pin: the resident path is taken and the local audit is not run when the resident is current; the fallback is taken when the resident's head differs from the local ref or the genesis differs; the act preflighted against the resident snapshot is the act submitted. 3. The security note in docs/reference/architecture.md, or the page that describes the resident trust boundary, states what the CLI accepts from the resident and what it still checks locally. 4. A measurement in the artifact text shows the wall time of one step command with and without the change at this workroom's depth. 5. go test ./... green at the exact head; independent review by codex; ratified; landed on main and pushed.","target_head":"3c7f13c79cb079ef0f40961d51d7ff4f350787c5","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}